  "feature": "Carrier LR/GR consignment documents linked to booking and exact POD version",
  "status": "Implemented and locally verified",
  "behavior": [
    "Truck Owners and Transporters may issue LR or GR for their confirmed assigned booking, before the first POD and while no dispute is open.",
    "Carrier document number/type/date are immutable; numbers are unique per carrier and Indian financial year. Both LR and GR use this same uniqueness rule.",
    "Party addresses, optional GSTIN/invoice/e-way bill references, packages, declared goods value and carrier authority attestation are captured.",
    "Goods, weight, route, vehicle, driver and gross freight come from the canonical booking/load and are frozen in each issued version.",
    "Amendments require the current version and a recorded reason. Earlier versions and optional private scans are retained.",
    "Stale versions conflict; a repeated identical request ID returns its prior issued version. Different details cannot reuse that ID.",
    "Each version has a printable HTML download and optional PDF/JPG/PNG carrier scan. Downloads are private to the parties and existing scoped dispute reviewers.",
    "POD freezes the exact current LR/GR version. A stale client reference fails; issuance/amendment and POD share booking row locks.",
    "Historical PODs retain no LR/GR reference. A later document cannot be backfilled into an earlier POD.",
    "POD replacement/review is transactional, preserving the prior file and removing a failed new upload. No freight settlement is inferred.",
    "Shipper, Truck Owner and Transporter Documents and Trip Details show the stored POD reference; the LR/GR Documents tab links to the exact booking.",
    "The shipper receives an issuance/amendment bell notification targeting the booking. Carrier issue controls are unavailable to the shipper.",
    "Strict staff access requires the existing POD capability plus a disputed-booking scope; admin downloads append a transactional Review audit event."
  ],
  "boundaries": {
    "documents": "Synthetic labelled QA scans and declared party particulars. No government, GST, e-way bill, signature or payment verification is claimed.",
    "download_format": "Printable self-contained HTML; carrier-supplied scans may be PDF, JPG or PNG. Generated PDF signing is not implemented.",
    "historical_data": "No historical LR/GR or POD links are invented. Documents recorded after departure are explicitly marked.",
    "payments": "Existing local mock booking-token flow only. No freight receipt or platform-fee collection was created in these cases.",
    "dispatch": "Existing document/payload and operator-route checks remain in force; LR/GR is not silently made a new requirement for every legacy booking."
  },
